{
  "analysis": "All three classes still fail on their smallest tertile (inclusion low-tertile recall 0.185, patches 0.478, scratches 0.377); missed medians (33.6/52.7/43.6 px) are ~0.4-0.6x the train medians. Round 1's prefer_small + 0.3/0.4 scale floors likely produced sub-learnable micro-pastes, so I raise the floor to 0.5 and use uniform weighting over sources that natively resemble the misses: short faint thin streaks (inclusion), small soft dark blobs (patches), thin bright vertical lines (scratches, incl. the high-contrast ones the model misses). Inclusion is worst (recall 0.285, 130 misses) so it gets the largest share; patches/scratches keep enough volume to avoid starving the shared detector.",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 28, "patches": 11, "scratches": 11},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.1, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [11, 150, 297, 50, 99, 106]},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.1, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [106, 39, 94, 63, 64, 240, 241, 251, 272, 51, 14, 161, 82, 182, 153, 65, 96, 86]},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.1, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [179, 180, 181, 182, 184, 185, 35, 36, 37, 41, 42, 43, 44, 52, 53, 57, 58, 91, 96, 19, 191, 192, 20, 200, 201, 203, 149, 169, 170, 133, 134, 112, 125]}
  },
  "rationale": "Shift from round 1: drop the 0.3/0.4 micro-scale floors (unlearnable pastes) and prefer_small, and instead paste appearance-matched sources (short faint streaks, small blobs, thin bright lines) at 0.5-1.1x so pastes land in the 25-70 px band of the missed instances. Inclusion gets 28 (worst recall, most misses, still under the ~80 diminishing-return threshold); patches/scratches get 11 each to keep the shared detector fed. All constraints satisfied: 28+11+11=50, within headroom (79/93/93) and cumulative caps (54/23/23 <=105), scale spans 0.6 >=0.2, >=2 sources each."
}

{
  "analysis": "Previews match the misses well. Inclusion pastes are thin faint streaks (vertical + a couple horizontal) at small-to-medium size, consistent with the 33.6px missed median and the low-contrast look. Patches pastes are soft dark blobs on textured gray/white backgrounds, matching the 52.7px missed blobs. Scratches pastes are thin bright lines (mostly vertical, some horizontal) matching the 43.6px missed lines including the brighter high-contrast ones the model fails on. No unrealistic or wasted pastes; sizes sit in the 25-70px band rather than sub-learnable micro-pastes. Plan stands.",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 28, "patches": 11, "scratches": 11},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.1, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [11, 150, 297, 50, 99, 106]},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.1, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [106, 39, 94, 63, 64, 240, 241, 251, 272, 51, 14, 161, 82, 182, 153, 65, 96, 86]},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.1, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [179, 180, 181, 182, 184, 185, 35, 36, 37, 41, 42, 43, 44, 52, 53, 57, 58, 91, 96, 19, 191, 192, 20, 200, 201, 203, 149, 169, 170, 133, 134, 112, 125]}
  },
  "rationale": "Preview confirms appearance-matched, learnable-sized pastes for all three classes (faint streaks / soft blobs / thin bright lines), targeting the small low-tertile misses without dropping into unlearnable micro-scales. Inclusion keeps the largest share (28) as the worst class; patches/scratches 11 each keep the shared detector fed. Constraints hold: 28+11+11=50, within headroom and cumulative caps, scale span 0.6>=0.2, >=2 sources each."
}
